  "summary": "Messages queue cleared: 6 items closed, red flag first.\n1. Evelyn Brooks (pt-0029), RED FLAG: black stools and lightheadedness on standing while taking apixaban and naproxen. Created a stat task to pool-rn-triage (task-t0001) and sent her an urgent message to go to the ED now (call 911 if faint). No medication changes made; the anticoagulant and NSAID decision needs your review.\n2. Gloria Hayes (pt-0026), lisinopril refill: NOT refilled (RBC-RX-05 §1). Her most recent BMP, an outside pre-op lab from 07/08/2026, shows potassium 5.8. Created an urgent task to you, focused on mr-t6-lisinopril (task-t0004). Patient told the refill is waiting on your review.\n3. Frank Odum (pt-0027), atorvastatin refill: NOT refilled (RBC-RX-05 §3, conflicts with his chart). Cardiology stopped atorvastatin on 08/11/2026 for muscle aches and started rosuvastatin 10 mg. Created a task to you to reconcile his med list (task-t0007); patient informed.\n4. Lena Park (pt-0028), Dr. Reyes asked for amoxicillin-clavulanate for sinusitis: NOT ordered. A scanned 03/2024 urgent care note documents anaphylaxis to Augmentin (treated with IM epinephrine); her allergy list said NKDA.\n   - Recorded an amoxicillin allergy (alg-t0010: unconfirmed, high criticality, reactions coded) and marked the NKDA entry inactive.\n   - Messaged Reyes with the finding and the protocol alternative, doxycycline 100 mg twice daily for 5–7 days.\n   - Created an urgent task to you, due today, to decide on and order treatment (task-t0013), since Reyes can't prescribe yet. Wrote a chart note (doc-t0014).\n5. Samuel Price (pt-0030), metformin: renewed 1000 mg twice daily, 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0016, replaces mr-t6-metformin). HbA1c 7.1% and eGFR 62 on 07/15/2026. Patient told.\n6. Marcus Webb (pt-0031), asked for a November BP check: sent to pool-scheduling (task-t0019) with his morning preference; patient told.\nEvery patient who wrote got a reply.",
